# Phase 8 Walkthrough — Frontend Architecture & Real-Time IDE

## 1. What & Why It Was Built

In Phases 1 through 7, we built the entire distributed backend: Express API, Docker sandboxing, BullMQ asynchronous workers, Redis cache-aside, dead-letter queues, optimistic concurrency locking, and rate limiting.

In **Phase 8**, we brought this system to life with an interview-grade, LeetCode-equivalent **Frontend Web Application** built with **React 19**, **Vite**, **TypeScript**, and **Monaco Editor** (VS Code web runtime).

### Key Features Built:
1. **Bespoke Modern Dark Design System (`client/src/index.css`)**:
   - Curated obsidian/slate color palette (`#090d16`, `#0f172a`, `#141e33`) with glowing gradient accents (Emerald `#10b981`, Indigo `#6366f1`, Cyan `#06b6d4`, Rose `#f43f5e`, Amber `#f59e0b`).
   - Glassmorphic panels (`backdrop-filter: blur(16px)`), customized sleek scrollbars, and pulsing micro-animations.
   - Professional typography featuring Google Fonts: **Inter** for UI controls and **JetBrains Mono** for code and technical stats.

2. **Split-Pane Problem Solving Workspace (`src/pages/ProblemDetailPage.tsx`)**:
   - **Left Column**: Problem statement, formatted constraints, sample test cases with one-click copy buttons, and an interactive "Submissions" tab.
   - **Right Column**: Language selector (`Python 3`, `C++ 17`, `Java 21`), starter code templates, embedded Monaco editor with dark theme syntax highlighting, and execution control deck.

3. **Real-Time Submission Polling Engine (`src/hooks/useSubmissionPolling.ts`)**:
   - When a user submits code, `POST /api/submissions` returns `201 Created` with status `'QUEUED'` in ~10ms.
   - The custom hook initiates non-blocking background polling at 1-second intervals against `GET /api/submissions/:id`.
   - The UI displays an animated loader during `QUEUED` and `RUNNING`, transitioning seamlessly to the terminal verdict card (`ACCEPTED`, `WRONG_ANSWER`, `TIME_LIMIT_EXCEEDED`, `COMPILATION_ERROR`, etc.) once the Docker worker finishes.

4. **Detailed Verdict & Telemetry Deck (`src/components/VerdictCard.tsx`)**:
   - Color-coded verdict badge.
   - Runtime execution clock (`297 ms`) and memory consumption meter (`16 MB`).
   - Compiler/runtime error traces rendered inside an obsidian code block.
   - Individual test case pass/fail breakdown chips.

5. **Authentication & Session Persistence (`src/context/AuthContext.tsx`)**:
   - JWT session management in `localStorage` with Axios request interceptors automatically attaching `Bearer <token>`.
   - One-click demo credentials autofill (`user@codejudge.com` / `user123` and `admin@codejudge.com` / `admin123`) on `/login`.
   - Protected routes for `/submissions`.

6. **Problem Catalog & Personal Submissions Log (`src/pages/ProblemsPage.tsx`, `src/pages/SubmissionsPage.tsx`)**:
   - Real-time search query filtering and difficulty tab filters (`All`, `Easy`, `Medium`, `Hard`).
   - Pagination controls, difficulty badges, and resource constraint indicators.

