## 3. Trade-offs & Engineering Decisions

| Architectural Choice | Decision Made | Trade-Off / Alternative Considered |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Real-time Updates** | Client Polling (1s interval, 60s timeout safeguard) | WebSockets / SSE offer instant push notifications, but require stateful socket gateway servers, sticky sessions, or Redis Pub/Sub socket adapters. Polling keeps API instances 100% stateless. |
| **Styling Engine** | Bespoke CSS Design System (`index.css`) with tokens | Avoided TailwindCSS configuration overhead, version mismatch, or bloated class names. Bespoke CSS gave pixel-perfect control over glowing gradients, Monaco wrappers, and glassmorphism. |
| **Editor Runtime** | `@monaco-editor/react` | Monaco is heavier than simple textareas or CodeMirror (~300KB gzipped), but delivers an authentic VS Code desktop editing experience expected by candidates in technical interviews. |
| **Token Storage** | `localStorage` | In high-security banking apps, `httpOnly` cookies with CSRF tokens prevent XSS token theft. For standard developer platforms, `localStorage` simplifies client-side state inspection and cross-origin dev proxying. |

